> Johanna holds a master’s from Columbia University in climate science where she sits on the board of the Graduate School of Arts and Science. Johanna also contributed a book, Environmental Debt: The Hidden Cost of a Changing Economy, which outlines a new framework for responsible business practices, connecting the ROI of business with sustainability. She is a skilled chef and avid foodie, advocating for a more sustainable food system. 
